  "notes": "Uptempo small-town anthem country — chant hooks, kid-and-family narratives, straight rock drive. The drums are the stated pattern: \"quarter kick under choruses and 8th hats; the uptempo cuts use a driving two-beat with hat opening on 4; ballads use cross-stick and light shaker,\" so the kick sits on all four beats and the open hat lands on beat 4. The entry adds one genuinely unusual claim — \"gang-vocal chorus layers double as a percussive element\" — which is authored as a clap/snap perc lane rather than as a vocal, because the engine has no vocal lane. The bass is quoted: \"8ths locked to the kick, quarters under verses,\" hence `mirror_kick` with a real anticipation figure. Harmony is \"I–IV–V and I–V–vi–IV with a ♭VII borrow on the rockers.\" Melody is \"mid-baritone, syllabic, narrow; the chorus is a repeated short cell designed for crowd singing,\" which is the high two-bar cell repeat against a narrow register. ⚠ Confidence is medium, matching the research; the per-track readings are marked [LOW-CONF] there. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the velocity tiers, the perc density and the counter ratio — \"driving\" and \"gang-vocal layers\" are directions, and 106–127 / 2–5 / 0.4 are this author's reading of them.",
